VeridianOS: meinproc: fail when the output cannot be written; drop deprecated libxml2 globals

GCC reported, for the VeridianOS cross build (libxml2 2.15.4):

- src/meinproc_common.cpp:76, :83, :108: ignoring return value of
  QFile::open [-Wunused-result]. Real bug: when meinproc6 could not open
  stdout, the --output file, index.html or one of the chunk files, the
  QFile::write() calls failed silently and meinproc6 still exited 0, so a
  documentation build "succeeded" with missing or partial HTML. doOutput()
  now logs the file and QFile::errorString() with the existing KDocToolsLog
  category and returns false, and meinproc6 dies with exit status 1 through
  its existing DIE() macro, like every other failure it reports.
- src/meinproc.cpp:188: 'xmlMemoryDump' is deprecated
  [-Wdeprecated-declarations]. In libxml2 2.15 the function body is empty
  ("This feature was removed"); remove the call. No behaviour change.
- libxml/parser.h:1356 (expanded from src/xslt.cpp): '__xmlIndentTreeOutput'
  is deprecated [-Wdeprecated-declarations]. KDocTools::transform() set the
  thread-local xmlIndentTreeOutput to the top-level stylesheet's indent
  value before xsltSaveResultTo(). libxml2 only consults that global when it
  serializes with format == 1, and libxslt passes format = (indent == 1)
  only for the "xml" output method (HTML/XHTML/text output never read it).
  So for every stylesheet whose top-level xsl:output sets indent, the result
  is identical without the assignment (indent="yes" -> global 1, which is
  also libxml2's default). It differs only for "xml"-method output: a
  stylesheet whose indent="yes" comes from an imported stylesheet while the
  top-level one leaves indent unset, and xsl:document / exsl:document
  results with indent="yes" (saved with their own style): libxslt already
  emitted the newlines but KDocTools suppressed the indentation spaces;
  both now follow the stylesheet as XSLT specifies. transform() also no
  longer leaves the calling thread's xmlIndentTreeOutput set to 0 for later
  libxml2 serializations. KDE's own stylesheets use the html and text
  methods, and meinproc6 and kio_help serialize nothing else, so they are
  unaffected. The deprecated global is no longer touched.

